<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Abdelkader</h1><p class="st-meta">1832 CE – 1847 CE · capital Mascara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Algerian state built by Emir Abdelkader to resist French conquest, a symbol of national resistance in modern Algeria.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beylik-of-the-west">Beylik of the West</a> collapsed, the tribes of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> chose the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir-abdelkader">Abdelkader</a> as their emir near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mascara-algeria">Mascara</a> in 1832. He fought the French and won recognition in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-desmichels">Treaty of Desmichels</a> of 1834 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tafna">Treaty of Tafna</a> of 1837.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir-abdelkader">Abdelkader</a> built a state with provincial governors, Islamic courts, regular taxes, a standing army and arsenals, moving his capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagdemt">Tagdemt</a>. At its height in the late 1830s, his authority covered most of western and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. He drew legitimacy from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and from resistance to the invaders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>War resumed in 1839, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-robert-bugeaud">Bugeaud</a>'s scorched-earth campaigns destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir-abdelkader">Abdelkader</a>'s towns; his mobile camp was captured in 1843. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco's</a> defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-isly">Isly</a> in 1844 cost him support, and he surrendered in 1847. Exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, he protected Christians during the 1860 massacres.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-abdelkader.jpg" alt="Emirate of Abdelkader" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Hierakares · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Emirate_of_Mascara.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1832 CE – 1847 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mascara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdelkader</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Sufi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Mascara, State of Abd al-Qadir</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=emirate-of-abdelkader" aria-label="Emirate of Abdelkader on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4683 898 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Abdelkader lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5003 1154L5003 1154M5003 1154L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5003 1154h0M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5003 1154h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5003 1154h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mascara. <a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=emirate-of-abdelkader">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
